{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-6-8","kind":"proposition","title":"直角三角形高线分出的两个三角形相似","englishTitle":"If in a right-angled triangle a perpendicular be drawn from the right angle to the base, the triangles adjoining the perpendicular are similar both to the whole and to one another.","book":6,"number":8,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":8,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":"https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷六"}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","contentId":"euclid-6-8","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"385cbc60f015e4a7d4def726cf9155c5a4af9ddab175f0c8d87bd51304df7e0d","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-6-8.statement","euclid-6-8.construction.1","euclid-6-8.proof.1","euclid-6-8.proof.2","euclid-6-8.proof.3","euclid-6-8.proof.4","euclid-6-8.proof.5","euclid-6-8.proof.6","euclid-6-8.proof.7","euclid-6-8.proof.8","euclid-6-8.proof.9","euclid-6-8.conclusion","euclid-6-8.historical.1","euclid-6-8.historical.2","euclid-6-8.historical.3","euclid-6-8.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-6-8.statement","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d5c43e8821cdbca58cd85c15da6395479bf73f2296e3d64562467e455e73868f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If in a right-angled triangle a perpendicular be drawn from the right angle to the base, the triangles adjoining the perpendicular are similar both to the whole and to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果在直角三角形时从直角到底边之间画上垂直的三角形,则垂直的三角形与整个和彼此相似。"},{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"直角三边形从直角向对边作一垂线分本形为两直角三边形即两形皆与全形相似亦自相似"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"在直角三角形中，从直角画一条垂线到对边，将原图形分成两个直角三角形，这意味着两个形状都与整体形状相似，并且本质上是相似的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"85a245c05e235844d1f63dd1f99a3d71c55fee04cd329dc71e91a12d2a1d2982","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let ABC be a right-angled triangle having the angle BAC right, and let AD be drawn from A perpendicular to BC; I say that each of the triangles ABD, ADC is similar to the whole ABC and, further, they are similar to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让ABC成为直角三角形,直角,BAC,AD从A直直线划到BC;我说,每个三角形ABD,ADC与整个三角形ABC相似,而且它们彼此相似。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"36e67c5124c4d2fa7078aea06c2e99e729e1ed1a4c321b41b571987092edb4a7","citations":["euclid-1-32"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since the angle BAC is equal to the angle ADB, for each is right, and the angle at B is common to the two triangles ABC and ABD, therefore the remaining angle ACB is equal to the remaining angle BAD; [[I. 32](/principles/euclid-1-32)] therefore the triangle ABC is equiangular with the triangle ABD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为BAC角等于ADB角,每个角为直角,B角是两个三角形的ABC和ABD的常见角,因此其余的ACB角等于其余角BAD;因此,ABC三角形与ABD三角形为等角。 [[I. 32](/principles/euclid-1-32)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"519c9b74646dc70a0377f89b3c9ceac7a1aa86c92a0737bea6591fca2d6e636d","citations":["euclid-6-4"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore, as BC which subtends the right angle in the triangle ABC is to BA which subtends the right angle in the triangle ABD, so is AB itself which subtends the angle at C in the triangle ABC to BD which subtends the equal angle BAD in the triangle ABD, and so also is AC to AD which subtends the angle at B common to the two triangles. [[VI. 4](/principles/euclid-6-4)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,BC比,将三角ABC比BA的直角比,将三角ABD比直角等于AB比,将三角ABC比C角角对BAD比BD,将三角ABD等于AC比AD比AC比AD,将角对B比两个三角。 [[VI. 4](/principles/euclid-6-4)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d29ccba59780d254217d64f012b8dc5a97fc856fbc76725a168297e5d6662683","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the triangle ABC is both equiangular to the triangle ABD and has the sides about the equal angles proportional."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,三角形ABC是三角形ABD的等角,两边是等角成比例。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e33c3e6933865d5fafea1ed1b77b42440d46f0d492b004674b7c9f8b8bebd247","citations":["euclid-6-def-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the triangle ABC is similar to the triangle ABD. [[VI. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-6-def-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,三角形ABC与三角形ABD相似。 [[VI. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-6-def-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6105ac1251ed9143ffd7fac3f9bcfea398c9b42fb8f7699746c8349e5c287212","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that the triangle ABC is also similar to the triangle ADC; therefore each of the triangles ABD, ADC is similar to the whole ABC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明三角形ABC也与三角形ADC类似;因此,三角形ABD、ADC和整个ABC相似。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b6f46f133c2f3ef62744b9f0a6081dfaab2eac79026142eed22d7d119bbb3dbe","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say next that the triangles ABD, ADC are also similar to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"接下来我说,三角形ABD,ADC 也相似。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7e2dc952878fcbdf5221c96b588b6ac073413649f4d5ab98ed005768879d2549","citations":["euclid-1-32"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since the right angle BDA is equal to the right angle ADC, and moreover the angle BAD was also proved equal to the angle at C, therefore the remaining angle at B is also equal to the remaining angle DAC; [[I. 32](/principles/euclid-1-32)] therefore the triangle ABD is equiangular with the triangle ADC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为直角 BDA等于直角 ADC,而且BAD角度也证明等于C角度,因此B的剩余角度也等于DAC;因此三角形ABD是三角形ADC的等角。 [[I. 32](/principles/euclid-1-32)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"33c8b09a95c7fdde8e53e95338ac13fd9c6c5b23b05436a8869dbb0ad6257bc1","citations":["euclid-6-4","euclid-6-def-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore, as BD which subtends the angle BAD in the triangle ABD is to DA which subtends the angle at C in the triangle ADC equal to the angle BAD, so is AD itself which subtends the angle at B in the triangle ABD to DC which subtends the angle DAC in the triangle ADC equal to the angle at B, and so also is BA to AC, these sides subtending the right angles; [[VI. 4](/principles/euclid-6-4)] therefore the triangle ABD is similar to the triangle ADC. [[VI. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-6-def-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,BD比,将三角ABD至DA的角BAD相相向,将三角C的角相向,等于BAD等值,将三角ABD至DC的角相向,B比AD比,将三角ADC的角相向,ADC比B,BA比AC,这些侧相向,直角比值;因此,三角ABD与ADC类似。（相关点与线段：DAC） [[VI. 4](/principles/euclid-6-4)] [[VI. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-6-def-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d0def46992eb0b105b82d6bce6477450c524a884c436026a0e1ed896becf6c9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此命题得证。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":11,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0a4536f76a0d3175504f8ae7256d7d0b936542819734139e4119e17d05c81e5c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Porism. From this it is clear that, if in a right-angled triangle a perpendicular be drawn from the right angle to the base, the straight line so drawn is a mean proportional between the segments of the base. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"推论,从这一点可以明显看出,如果在直角三角形中从直角到底边之间划直线,那么在底边、Q、E、D之间划直线为比例中项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.historical.1","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":12,"kind":"historical_note","title":"徐光启、利玛窦历史中译 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d484f44e526194b17def23f16517ef7e9eefb6e11432c390b7e93477487e907d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"直角三边形从直角向对边作一垂线分本形为两直角三边形即两形皆与全形相似亦自相似"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"在直角三角形中，从直角画一条垂线到对边，将原图形分成两个直角三角形，这意味着两个形状都与整体形状相似，并且本质上是相似的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.historical.2","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":13,"kind":"historical_note","title":"徐光启、利玛窦历史中译 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"01b3973e08af125d73f9ba40ac95e738f10732c4320e43018678f6f3fabe86a6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"解曰：甲乙丙直角三边形从乙甲丙直角作甲丁垂线题言所分甲丁丙甲丁乙两三边形皆与全形相似亦自相似"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"解释如下：甲乙丙 直角三角形，从直角 乙甲丙 画一条垂线。甲丁 命题：被分割的三角形 甲丁丙甲丁乙 两个三角形都与整体形状相似，并且是自相似的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.historical.3","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":14,"kind":"historical_note","title":"徐光启、利玛窦历史中译 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"31373bea95b007418544be1b3d242b373f25fee3e4f4399fbf86dfe9bfefcb3d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"论曰：甲乙丙甲丁丙两形既各以乙甲丙甲丁丙为直角而丙角又同即其馀甲乙丙丁甲丙两角必等〈一卷三〉则甲乙丙甲丁丙两形必为等角形而等角旁之各两边比例必等等者谓乙丙与甲丙若甲丙与丙丁也甲丙与甲乙若丙丁与甲丁也乙丙与甲乙若甲丙与甲丁也即甲丁丙角形与甲乙丙全形相似矣〈本篇四〉依显甲丁乙角形与甲乙丙全形亦相似也何者丙甲乙甲丁乙两皆直角而乙角又同即其馀甲丙乙丁甲乙两角必等〈一卷卅二〉甲乙丙甲丁乙两形必为等角形而等角旁之各两边比例必等故也依显甲丁乙甲丁丙两角形亦相似也何者两形各与全形相似即两形自相似〈五卷十一〉系从直角作垂线即此线为两分对边线比例之中率而直角旁两边各为对角全边与同方分边比例之中率何者丙丁与丁甲之比例若丁甲与丁乙也故丁甲为丙丁丁乙两分边比例之中率也又乙丙与丙甲之比例若丙甲与丙丁也故丙甲为乙丙丙丁之中率也乙丙与乙甲之比例若乙甲与乙丁也故乙甲为乙丙乙丁之中率也"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"证明如下：甲乙丙甲丁丙: 由于 乙甲丙甲丁丙 是直角，且 丙 相同，那么其他 甲乙丙丁甲丙 角必须相等。〈一卷三〉 然后 甲乙丙甲丁丙 必须是全等三角形，并且每个角旁边的边的比例相等。这意味着 乙丙 和 甲丙；如果 甲丙 和 丙丁，甲丙 和 甲乙；如果 丙丁 和 甲丁，那么 乙丙 和 甲乙；如果 甲丙 和 甲丁，即 甲丁丙 和 甲乙丙 形状相似。〈本篇四〉 表明 甲丁乙 和 甲乙丙 也形状相等。为什么 丙甲乙甲丁乙 都是直角，而 乙 有相同的角，这意味着其他 甲丙乙丁甲乙 角必须相等 〈一卷卅二〉甲乙丙甲丁乙 甲丙乙丁甲乙 和这两个角必须相等 两个形状必须是全等三角形，并且等角旁边的每条边的比例必须相等。根据清楚的 甲丁乙甲丁丙，两三角形也相似。为什么两个形状各自与全形相似，这意味着两个形状是自相似的？〈五卷十一〉 从直角画出垂线；这条线是对边两边的中比，并且直角旁边边的中比是对角全边的中比和同边的边分比。丙丁 与 丁甲 的中比是多少？如果 丁甲 和 丁乙 是 丁乙，那么 丁甲 是 丙丁丁乙 与 丙丁丁乙 的中比，因此 丁甲 是 乙丙乙丁 的中比。"}]},{"id":"euclid-6-8.source","contentId":"euclid-6-8","revisionId":"euclid-6-8@raw-385cbc60f015e4a7","order":15,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0f0433686a7d91d30b163e6bfee7ce128a65a16ce69af655f5423fd45e195cd9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\nHistorical Chinese source: https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷六"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-6-8:euclid-1-32:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-6-8","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-6-8.proof.1","euclid-6-8.proof.7"],"targetContentId":"euclid-1-32","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8/","sourceLabel":"I. 32"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-6-8:euclid-6-4:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-6-8","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-6-8.proof.2","euclid-6-8.proof.8"],"targetContentId":"euclid-6-4","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8/","sourceLabel":"VI. 4"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-6-8:euclid-6-def-1:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-6-8","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-6-8.proof.4","euclid-6-8.proof.8"],"targetContentId":"euclid-6-def-1","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:6.prop.8/","sourceLabel":"VI. Def. 1"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-6-13:euclid-6-8:explicit","sourceContentId":